{
 "format": "damap",
 "version": 1,
 "id": "9a",
 "name": "Rock Trolls",
 "file": "Map9a_RockTrolls.xml",
 "rooms": [
  {"id":1,"x":60,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Journalai Route, Rolling Hills","descriptions":["The old, abandoned Journalai Route runs through the rolling hills outside of the village of Kaerna like a winding brownish-green ribbon someone dropped and forgot.  A few stones that might have been road markers still remain, cracked and weathered and lying, forsaken, to one side of the road."],"exits":[{"to":2,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":3,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":2,"x":80,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Journalai Route, Foothills","descriptions":["A set of rolling green hills rise up to the west, gradually flattening out into grasslands to the east.  A barricade blocks off further passage toward the east along the Journalai Route."],"exits":[{"to":1,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":36,"exit":"climb","move":"climb barricade"}]},
  {"id":3,"x":40,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Journalai Route, Rolling Hills","descriptions":["The Route continues to the east and west, while to the north you notice a dirt path that looks to have been tread by the passage of feet, not the passage of wagons.  A trickling stream passes over the road, leaving mud and muck in its wake as it vanishes into the grasses of the surrounding hillside."],"exits":[{"to":21,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":1,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":4,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":4,"x":-40,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Journalai Route, Rolling Hills","descriptions":["The silence here would be peaceful, if it weren't so intrusive.  No birdsong, no movement of wildlife, just an empty, all-encompassing stillness, as if the green, wild hills that rise about you were holding their breath."],"exits":[{"to":3,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":5,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":5,"x":-60,"y":40,"z":0,"title":"Journalai Route, Rolling Hills","descriptions":["From here, the top of one of the tallest hills, you can see the lay of the land, rising and falling before and behind you.  The Route winds onward to the east, and dwindles slowly toward the west."],"exits":[{"to":4,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":6,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":6,"x":-80,"y":40,"z":0,"title":"Journalai Route, Rolling Hills","descriptions":["Slender, willowy trees grow along the side of the road on this part of the Route, their boughs intertwining to form a wild, beautiful arch of leaf and branch.  From somewhere in the trees you hear the soft twitter of a single bird, the first you have heard in your entire time here."],"exits":[{"to":5,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":7,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":7,"x":-100,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Journalai Route, Rolling Hills","descriptions":["Large stones crop out from the sides of the hills, bones jutting from the round flesh of the earth.  Wild roses climb over the hillsides, their bushes tangling into one another, and their fresh scent encircling you.  It is not enough, however, to dispel the faint tinge of rot that seems to hang in the air."],"exits":[{"to":6,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":8,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":8,"x":-120,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Journalai Route, Rocky Hills","descriptions":["The ground is extremely stony here, and the sides of the hills are dotted with the broken remains of boulders.  To the west you see mountain peaks, broken-edged etchings against the sky.  Patches of grass grow sporadically amongst the gravel and stones through which you pick your way, and it is hard to distinguish where the sides of the Route end, and where the hills begin."],"exits":[{"to":7,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":9,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":9,"x":-160,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Journalai Route, Rockslide","descriptions":["A massive rockslide has cut off any further western passage along the Journalai Route by caravan, and the slide itself looks too unstable and massive to climb safely.  You can catch a glimpse of sweeping forested mountainside just beyond the barrier, the caps of the peaks frosted with eternal snows."],"exits":[{"to":8,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":10,"exit":"climb","move":"climb path"},{"to":22,"exit":"go","move":"go rockslide"}]},
  {"id":10,"x":-160,"y":-40,"z":0,"title":"Rolling Hills","descriptions":["Mountains to the west loom protectively over their smaller siblings, the hills.  Somewhere to the northeast you can catch the occasional splishing sound that signals the presence of a river or stream nearby."],"exits":[{"to":11,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":9,"exit":"climb","move":"climb path"}]},
  {"id":11,"x":-120,"y":-40,"z":0,"title":"Rolling Hills","descriptions":["The hills shoulder the Route, observing all that passes down its fading trail with silent, unseen eyes."],"exits":[{"to":12,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":10,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":12,"x":-100,"y":-60,"z":0,"title":"Rolling Hills, Rocky Slope","descriptions":["The ground is sprinkled with bits of gravel and stone, making this steep slope an adventure in and of itself.  Split boulders strewn across the ground prove to be good for catching your balance when dexterity gives way to gravity and the slippery mixture of skree and grass."],"exits":[{"to":11,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":13,"exit":"down","move":"down"}]},
  {"id":13,"x":-100,"y":-40,"z":0,"title":"Rolling Hills, A Sheltered Vale","descriptions":["The grass grows in lush clumps beneath your feet, carpeting the tiny hillocks that rise up from the ground.  A butterfly floats through the air as it makes its way from wildflower to wildflower, its wings bright and vivid."],"exits":[{"to":14,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":12,"exit":"up","move":"up"}]},
  {"id":14,"x":-80,"y":-40,"z":0,"title":"Rolling Hills, A Sheltered Vale","descriptions":["The grass grows in a dark, soft circle here, inviting you to rest and relax, while tall wiir trees make a ring around the patch of green, their boughs intertwining in defense against the wind and rain.  An opening in a set of rocks piled up by the side of a hill creates a cave-like shelter to further protect you from the elements."],"exits":[{"to":15,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":13,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":37,"exit":"go","move":"go cave"}]},
  {"id":15,"x":-60,"y":-60,"z":0,"title":"Rolling Hills, A Sheltered Vale","descriptions":["The grass grows thick and lush beneath your feet, while above you rise tall wiir trees in full flourish.  The only disturbances are a set of large, unusual footprints that have crushed the tall grass, and the long marks, as if something heavy had been dragged through here, that accompany them."],"exits":[{"to":14,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":16,"exit":"up","move":"up"}]},
  {"id":16,"x":-60,"y":-80,"z":0,"title":"Rolling Hills, Green Slope","descriptions":["Dazzling green hues spread over the surrounding hillside, creating a rippling illusion of movement.  The side of the hill you stand on slopes downward toward a tiny vale, while to the east it climbs back toward a dip where several hills meet."],"exits":[{"to":17,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":15,"exit":"down","move":"down"}]},
  {"id":17,"x":-40,"y":-80,"z":0,"title":"Rolling Hills, Grassy Knoll","descriptions":["The hills rise like frozen waves, their slopes leading down to a grassy knoll, as if in homage to something or someone.  A brisk breeze gusts downs from the high, untouched hilltops, creating a lonely song that whistles through the stones of the knoll."],"exits":[{"to":18,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":16,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":18,"x":-20,"y":-60,"z":0,"title":"Rolling Hills, Clear Pool","descriptions":["The hills close in about you, monuments to greenery and life.  A pool is cupped at the base of one of the hills, its surface constantly moving from unseen currents.  A good-size hole opens up in the ground by one of the largest, steepest hills.  It leads down into darkness, giving no hint of where it might go."],"exits":[{"to":17,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":19,"exit":"go","move":"go hole"},{"to":38,"exit":"go","move":"go pool"}],"aliases":["Clear Pool","Pool"]},
  {"id":19,"x":0,"y":-40,"z":0,"title":"Rolling Hills, Inside the Log","descriptions":["The log is surprisingly large inside, big enough for an Elf to crouch in without being cramped.  The faint scent of rot that fills it does not make it a pleasant place to stay, however, and you feel oddly relieved that it is too dark in here to tell exactly what it is you are stepping in that squishes so."],"exits":[{"to":18,"exit":"up","move":"up"},{"to":20,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"aliases":["Log"]},
  {"id":20,"x":20,"y":-20,"z":0,"title":"Rolling Hills, Trickling Stream","descriptions":["The stream splashes its way southeast, springing forth from underneath a set of rocks that jut out of the hill in front of you.  A hollow log lies next to the creek, looking a tad out of place in this mostly treeless land."],"exits":[{"to":21,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":19,"exit":"go","move":"go log"}]},
  {"id":21,"x":40,"y":0,"z":0,"title":"Rolling Hills, Trickling Stream","descriptions":["A dirt path cuts its way along the grassy bank of a thin stream, winding northwards to untamed hills, and southward back to the Journalai Route.  The size of the stream's bed suggests that it must have been bigger once, but upheaval has changed it to a fraction of the size it used to be."],"exits":[{"to":3,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":20,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":22,"x":-200,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Journalai Route, Rocky Pass","descriptions":["High walls of stone rise up on either side of the rocky pass as this hidden spur of the Journalai Route branches off toward forested mountain slopes.  Small clumps of heather find unreliable purchase alongside the road where time and nature have pulverized the fallen boulders to ragged piles of gravel."],"exits":[{"to":23,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":9,"exit":"go","move":"go rockslide"}]},
  {"id":23,"x":-220,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Journalai Route, Rocky Pass","descriptions":["Westward, the high stone walls close in more tightly overhead, completely blocking the view of the nearby mountains.  A chance avalanche would be disastrous for anyone passing along the road."],"exits":[{"to":22,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":24,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":24,"x":-240,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Journalai Route, Rocky Pass","descriptions":["The walls are barely shoulder-width here, closing out all but a narrow strip of sky above.  Shattered slabs of fallen granite clog most of the path and stray breezes bring showers of tiny pebbles and stone dust from above.  The faint light makes maneuvering difficult as the fallen boulders appear no more than vague shadows within the gloom."],"exits":[{"to":23,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":25,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":25,"x":-260,"y":40,"z":0,"title":"Journalai Route, Shadowy Cul-de-sac","descriptions":["The road ends in this dark cul-de-sac, providing no visible means of escape for anyone caught unaware from behind.  Scattered bones from some unidentifiable victim gleam softly in the darkness.  Deep shadows surround the perimeter of the area and the faint scent of burning charcoal hangs in the air."],"exits":[{"to":24,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":26,"exit":"go","move":"go trail"}]},
  {"id":26,"x":-280,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Journalai Route, Dim Passage","descriptions":["The dim passage is a good deal larger than it looks from a distance.  From the texture of the walls and the chips of granite covering the floor, it's apparent the tunnel is not a natural formation.  Someone carved a trail between the cul-de-sac and whatever lies beyond the wall."],"exits":[{"to":27,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":25,"exit":"go","move":"go trail"}]},
  {"id":27,"x":-300,"y":40,"z":0,"title":"Limestone Valley, Dim Tunnel","descriptions":["The path underfoot is treacherous and strewn with gravel chips painstakingly carved from the rock wall.  This end of the tunnel opens through a granite arch onto a limestone valley.  The scent of burning charcoal is much stronger here."],"exits":[{"to":26,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":28,"exit":"go","move":"go arch"}]},
  {"id":28,"x":-320,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Limestone Valley, Granite Arch","descriptions":["A granite arch opens into the base of an unusual stone wall.  Nearly thirty feet tall, the granite wall is encrusted with shimmering quartz crystals.  Although the crystals have been removed as high as can be readily reached, the remaining strip extends along the southern wall of the valley in brilliant display."],"exits":[{"to":35,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":29,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":27,"exit":"go","move":"go arch"}]},
  {"id":29,"x":-340,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Limestone Valley, Marble Vein","descriptions":["Between the crystal-encrusted granite and the chalky lime runs a thick vein of pure ivory marble.  An ambitious Halfling miner was unsuccessful in attempts to reap some of nature's bounty before being overcome by the fumes.  Nothing but a skeleton and a few tattered scraps of clothing are left."],"exits":[{"to":28,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":30,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":30,"x":-360,"y":0,"z":0,"title":"Limestone Valley, Western Wall","descriptions":["The path here is thick with spatters from the pit, making each step a challenge.  An extremely large bubble of tar hisses and burbles, slowly releasing a steady stream of gas and black ooze."],"exits":[{"to":31,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":29,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}]},
  {"id":31,"x":-340,"y":-20,"z":0,"title":"Limestone Valley, Northern Wall","descriptions":["The skeleton of a mid-size feline lies here in disarray and several large chunks of limestone are shattered beneath the remains.  It appears the edge of the cliff gave way while the luckless animal investigated the valley from above.  A far quicker death than the slowly suffocating fumes of the pit."],"exits":[{"to":32,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":30,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":32,"x":-320,"y":-20,"z":0,"title":"Limestone Valley, Marble Gate","descriptions":["A tall arch is carved into the wall and set with a solid marble gate.  Although there's no apparent locking mechanism, the gate is solidly closed.  Fresh air drifts through the narrow crack around the slab carrying a hint of pine."],"exits":[{"to":33,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":31,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":33,"x":-300,"y":-20,"z":0,"title":"Limestone Valley, Northern Wall","descriptions":["Thin striations of pure pink marble can be seen embedded in the limestone.  The veins are scarce, but time will create a rich harvest for future miners."],"exits":[{"to":34,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":32,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":34,"x":-280,"y":0,"z":0,"title":"Limestone Valley, Eastern Wall","descriptions":["The greyish-white wall leans in over the tar pit where the path narrows to a few feet across.  A fine rain of chalky powder continually drifts down from above, dislodged by stray breezes."],"exits":[{"to":35,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":33,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":35,"x":-300,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Limestone Valley, Crystal Wall","descriptions":["The crystals end abrubtly at the eastern wall of the valley, refracting pinpoints of light against a limestone backdrop.  The slight inward tilt of the limestone cliffs precludes any possibility of scaling them."],"exits":[{"to":34,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":28,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":36,"x":100,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Journalai Route, Open Grasslands","descriptions":["The grasslands here are caught between the presence of rolling hills to the west and the small village of Kaerna to the east.  To the north and south is nothing but empty plains, wind-twisted and long ignored by humanity."],"exits":[{"to":0,"exit":"east","move":"east"}],"linksTo":"Map7_NTR_Part1.xml"},
  {"id":37,"x":-80,"y":-20,"z":0,"title":"Rolling Hills, Inside a Small Cave","descriptions":["The floor of the cave is sandy, while the back of it seems to be made of dirt.  It is relatively small, but well-lit, its opening leading out into a lush vale.  A small firering composed of blackened stones and cold ashes occupies the center of the cave."],"exits":[{"to":14,"exit":"out","move":"out"}]},
  {"id":38,"x":-20,"y":-40,"z":0,"title":"A Clear Pool","descriptions":["Around you stand the high hills of the countryside, their broken reflections rippling in the pool, while all about you spreads cool, cold water, running deep and moving slowly with unseen currents.  From time to time a bubble pops on the surface, creating a gentle stir over the water."],"exits":[{"to":18,"exit":"out","move":"out"}]}
 ],
 "labels": [
  {"text":"Rock Trolls","x":-100,"y":-10,"z":0},
  {"text":"Rock Trolls","x":-350,"y":-50,"z":0},
  {"text":"NTR Part 1","x":90,"y":30,"z":0},
  {"text":"Journalai Route","x":-199,"y":26,"z":0}
 ]
}
